## TUI syntax highlighting and tool-output presentation — 2026-11-16

- Removed duplicate legacy Markdown/highlighter declarations that conflicted with the active Chroma renderer. Replaced heuristic keyword coloring with Chroma grammar-based tokenization and Aichat-style line-by-line highlighting; code fences and their info strings remain visible, source text is preserved, leading indentation is retained, and shell shebangs are inferred when no language is specified.
- Streaming Markdown now resolves a code fence's lexer once and reuses it for each completed line instead of re-tokenizing the full accumulated block for every line. Closing fences reset the lexer state. The renderer keeps Chroma's Monokai/terminal-256 palette; this is the Go-native equivalent path, not a linked Syntect runtime.
- Shell tool events display one `$ <command>` row followed by the raw captured output. Removed redundant “tool output” headings and duplicate command/completion summaries; shell and trajectory output in both scrollback and full-screen/history paths use a dedicated ANSI-256 dark-grey foreground (color 240).
